---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';

const flexModelHref = withBase('/research/FlexFacets.tla');
---

<section id="case-studies" class="case-studies" aria-label="Three studies">
  <article id="study-a" class="article-body study" aria-labelledby="study-a-title">
    <h2 id="study-a-title">Study A: What can an item-local rule certify about flexbox?</h2>
    <p class="study-status">Bounded positive result. Finite models, exact arithmetic, and browser perturbation across real pages.</p>
    <p>Finite browser probes across 1,200 rendered pages found no sibling coupling in 45.76% of 2,255 eligible flex containers. The item-local predicate certifies 28.07% of them.</p>
    <figure class="coverage-figure">
      <figcaption>Share of 2,255 eligible flex containers</figcaption>
      <div><label for="observed-coverage">No coupling detected <strong>45.76%</strong></label><meter id="observed-coverage" min="0" max="100" value="45.76">45.76%</meter></div>
      <div><label for="certified-coverage">Certified by the local predicate <strong>28.07%</strong></label><meter id="certified-coverage" class="certified" min="0" max="100" value="28.07">28.07%</meter></div>
    </figure>
    <p>Observation is not certification. The predicate is sound and maximal on eight checked finite domains, not for arbitrary CSS, and the 17.69-point gap remains an open question about what information an item-local rule cannot see. A precise bounded claim is more useful than a broad guarantee the evidence cannot carry.</p>
    <p><a class="study-link" href={flexModelHref} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Inspect the TLA+ model <Icon name="file" size={16} /></a></p>
  </article>

  <article id="study-b" class="article-body study" aria-labelledby="study-b-title">
    <h2 id="study-b-title">Study B: Can a policy account for what a build actually publishes?</h2>
    <p class="study-status">Single-repository finding. An abstract disclosure model paired with inspection of emitted files.</p>
    <p>The policy declares 12 output sinks and 11 source-to-sink flows. Checking only the policy, or only the emitted bytes, does not establish publication safety, so the study checks both.</p>
    <p>Doing so exposed two gaps. A reversible representation bypassed a literal check, and two published PDFs sat outside the prior audit set. The case establishes existence, not prevalence. Boundaries fail where ownership and inventories drift.</p>
  </article>

  <article id="study-c" class="article-body study" aria-labelledby="study-c-title">
    <h2 id="study-c-title">Study C: Does TLA+-guided repair improve an LLM-generated web artifact?</h2>
    <p class="study-status">Negative feasibility result. One paid task, generated behavioral contracts, browser replay, and bounded repair.</p>
    <p>The run made 13 provider requests with no retries and recorded 349,968 input and output tokens. The fresh baseline received 58/100, while the TLA+-guided run was blocked before repair and remained unscored.</p>
    <p>Offline, ordinary depth-12 search matched the synthetic TLC witness with the same 12 browser actions. Until the formal path shows value beyond that search, another paid run is not justified. Stop an expensive direction when its incremental value remains unestablished, and preserve the negative result.</p>
  </article>

  <div class="article-body">
    <h2>What these studies do not establish</h2>
    <p>These studies do not establish a general guarantee. The finite models, corpus observations, single-repository audit, and one-task feasibility result each support a different, bounded conclusion.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .case-studies {
    padding-bottom: 24px;
    scroll-margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .study {
    margin-top: 32px;
    padding-top: 8px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    scroll-margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .article-body > p.study-status {
    margin-top: 10px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font: 500 16px/1.5 var(--sans);
  }

  .coverage-figure {
    margin: 28px 0 8px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
  }

  .coverage-figure figcaption {
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .coverage-figure > div + div {
    margin-top: 14px;
  }

  .coverage-figure label {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 16px;
  }

  .coverage-figure strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .coverage-figure meter {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 10px;
    margin-top: 6px;
    border: 0;
    background: var(--panel-2);
  }

  .coverage-figure meter::-webkit-meter-bar { background: var(--panel-2); border: 0; border-radius: 0; }
  .coverage-figure meter::-webkit-meter-optimum-value { background: #8a9199; }
  .coverage-figure meter::-moz-meter-bar { background: #8a9199; }
  .coverage-figure meter.certified::-webkit-meter-optimum-value { background: var(--accent); }
  .coverage-figure meter.certified::-moz-meter-bar { background: var(--accent); }

  .study-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    min-height: 44px;
  }

  .study-link :global(svg) {
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
</style>